prompt:
We have a limited slate to fill this year: the curator can only greenlight a handful of exhibition themes. The job is to pick which few to go ahead with so that, when counting every unique visitor who’d attend at least one of the chosen shows, that headcount is maximized — overlaps between shows shouldn’t be double-counted. A better choice is simply the one that brings in the most different people overall, given the cap on how many themes we can run. The concrete theme options and their expected audiences are listed below.

